WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.465
The respiratory act comprises four phases. Therefore, first we learn to...

2
00:00:04.465 --> 00:00:09.235
I am conscious of my respiration, and then I am conscious of following my

3
00:00:09.235 --> 00:00:09.995
respiration.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.300
First, you bring mindfulness to the respiration.

5
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.024
Within mindfulness, there is also an energy we call concentration.

6
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.987
Because automatically, I must remain attentive for a longer duration.

7
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.790
Attempt to perceive this.

8
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.660
Scientific research indicates that by working at this level,

9
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.400
you develop empathic faculties, compassion, and attention,

10
00:00:37.011 --> 00:00:39.781
far more subtle, which lead to a state of well-being.

11
00:00:39.781 --> 00:00:43.861
What I refer to as joy, when one learns to remain focused on their respiration,

12
00:00:43.861 --> 00:00:47.041
when one learns to follow their respiration, subsequently,

13
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:49.874
one learns to recognize the body, uniting body and mind,

14
00:00:49.874 --> 00:00:53.764
and then, at the fourth level, one learns to release the body.

15
00:00:53.891 --> 00:00:56.771
Once this is accomplished, we delve into the essence.

16
00:00:56.771 --> 00:01:01.191
The fifth level is to generate a feeling of joy, which is said to originate from the teachings

17
00:01:01.191 --> 00:01:06.431
of the Buddha, who stated, 'I will teach you 16 ways to engender respiration.

18
00:01:06.431 --> 00:01:11.591
' And then, we will perform an exercise that focuses more on the expiratory act,

19
00:01:12.222 --> 00:01:15.172
which is called 'Brah-mari,' the bee's breath.

20
00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:20.262
This has a very interesting faculty on the brain, rapidly inducing a calm state of

21
00:01:20.262 --> 00:01:22.652
the mind and a reduction in stress.

22
00:01:24.213 --> 00:01:28.350
The tongue is the bud of the heart, and the thyroid originates from the tongue.

23
00:01:28.393 --> 00:01:32.193
One speaks with their heart, in fact, but with the frequential,

24
00:01:32.193 --> 00:01:35.621
almost energetic, subtlety, one might say, of the thyroid.

25
00:01:35.713 --> 00:01:39.113
This implies that at a certain point, it is no longer the word itself,

26
00:01:39.113 --> 00:01:40.033
but the sound.

27
00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.889
It is the frequency you engage with.

28
00:01:41.889 --> 00:01:44.619
I will guide you; we will perform the first five steps,

29
00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:48.789
then we will do the Brah-mari, and then we will release and simply observe a kind of

30
00:01:48.789 --> 00:01:49.764
silence within the body.

31
00:01:49.764 --> 00:01:53.165
One will need to produce a sound originating from the posterior pharynx.

32
00:01:53.165 --> 00:01:57.655
Like a bee or a bumblebee ascending, and this sound must rise into the cavity to

33
00:01:57.655 --> 00:01:59.683
culminate at the level of the sinuses.

34
00:01:59.824 --> 00:02:04.734
We will assess the entire cerebral region, extending into the tympanic cavity and

35
00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:05.427
sinus cavity.

36
00:02:06.064 --> 00:02:09.264
Frontal, sphenoidal, maxillary, and even temporal.

37
00:02:09.264 --> 00:02:11.379
We will first adopt an upright posture.

38
00:02:11.444 --> 00:02:16.794
When I straighten my back, upon exhalation, I will experience the true physiological

39
00:02:16.794 --> 00:02:19.044
effect of a release on my vagal tone.

40
00:02:20.355 --> 00:02:22.935
this parasympathetic and restorative system.

41
00:02:22.935 --> 00:02:27.124
If I position myself thus, and restrict here, I diminish this capacity.

42
00:02:27.124 --> 00:02:30.314
I experience this state of inspiratory awareness.

43
00:02:30.795 --> 00:02:35.675
Second level, I am very, very attentive to the act of respiration.

44
00:02:36.935 --> 00:02:41.545
I am aware of the body's movement during the respiratory act.

45
00:02:41.545 --> 00:02:42.863
Fourth level, I relax.

46
00:02:42.935 --> 00:02:46.165
upon exhalation, fully conscious that I am inhaling.

47
00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:48.403
We will perform twelve respirations.

48
00:02:48.426 --> 00:02:52.886
the first two we will perform thus, and the last ten we will perform with the ears

49
00:02:52.886 --> 00:02:56.746
slightly occluded; you will place your fingers over your ears

50
00:02:57.026 --> 00:03:01.956
to facilitate internal integration; you inhale, and during the expiratory phase,

51
00:03:01.956 --> 00:03:03.882
you produce a gentle humming sound.

52
00:03:13.066 --> 00:03:17.266
we inhale, occlude the ears, and you perform this ten times,

53
00:03:17.266 --> 00:03:18.926
and then you may release; you

54
00:03:22.677 --> 00:03:26.427
enter into the emerging silence, and within this silence,

55
00:03:26.427 --> 00:03:31.567
you simply allow a feeling of joy to arise, and if you are unsure what to do,

56
00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:32.437
offer a small

57
00:03:34.837 --> 00:03:38.287
smile; take another inhalation, perform an exhalation,

58
00:03:38.287 --> 00:03:44.117
and at the conclusion of the exhalation, There is a space where you do not respire.

59
00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.940
But you settle your consciousness within this space.

60
00:03:52.848 --> 00:03:55.920
Even as you reinspire, you remain within this space.

61
00:03:56.868 --> 00:04:01.578
When you enter this perception, you bring yourself closer to the embryonic breath.

62
00:04:05.368 --> 00:04:09.658
Because the embryonic breath was not subject to diaphragmatic movements.

63
00:04:10.228 --> 00:04:13.408
And if you do so, you will begin to perceive your heart,

64
00:04:13.408 --> 00:04:17.748
which was there eight months and nine days before your thoracic respiration.

65
00:04:23.799 --> 00:04:28.009
In other words, your heart begins to beat after 21 days.

66
00:04:29.319 --> 00:04:31.899
And so it is good to place oneself, from time to time,

67
00:04:31.899 --> 00:04:36.022
in this silence, because it is in silence that reorganization can occur.

68
00:04:36.022 --> 00:04:39.792
This embryonic force is always present, but to enter into this presence,

69
00:04:39.792 --> 00:04:42.572
this contact, you must accept to go into silence.

70
00:04:42.572 --> 00:04:44.612
You might rediscover a healing movement.

71
00:04:44.612 --> 00:04:47.175
Or that health can express itself, flourish more

72
00:04:47.175 --> 00:04:47.755
easily.

73
00:04:47.755 --> 00:04:51.125
You place it in this silence and allow space to open.

74
00:04:51.125 --> 00:04:52.932
Thus, a need for space.

75
00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:57.870
If there is no space, there is no development. Therefore, both this

76
00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:01.460
spacious silence are required.

77
00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:07.150
But if you restore to the tissue this capacity to rediscover this moment of silence,

78
00:05:10.341 --> 00:05:14.561
the body knows very well how it should reorganize itself because there it can

79
00:05:14.561 --> 00:05:17.333
utilize its potential upon which it was created.

80
00:05:17.333 --> 00:05:21.553
Therefore, I restore the possibility to the system that it knows,

81
00:05:21.553 --> 00:05:24.643
but it is so occupied that it no longer knows.

82
00:05:24.643 --> 00:05:26.723
I restore this vital principle.

83
00:05:27.721 --> 00:05:29.881
je redonne ce principe vital

